	// includes/sync/class-sync-manifest.php (Z8b branch 4, V5: the clock of the manifest)
	'The clock of this site gives no time (a whole number of seconds), so no package is signed or read: whether a package is still valid is decided by its time only. Try again; if it keeps failing, ask the host to check the clock of the server.',
	// includes/sync/class-sync-code-stage.php (Z8b branch 4, Behebung 1: a stage without its run, bytes not of the manifest, a head not read whole)
	'A stage belongs to a run of the takeover: pass its run_id, a whole number of 1 or more. Nothing was fetched or written.',
	'%s did not read whole as the manifest of the stage names it (its size and SHA-256), so it is not checked and the stage is never ready. Stage the unit again.',
	'The head of %s in the new version could not be read whole, so what it requires is not known and it is not swapped. Stage the unit again.',
	// includes/sync/class-sync-code-stage.php (Z8b branch 4, Behebung 2: no time to measure a call by)
	'The time of this call could not be measured, so nothing of the unit was read or taken. Call again.',
	// includes/sync/class-sync-engine.php (Z8b branch 5, V12 of its pre-check: the way back of a step whose pair was discarded since, or cannot be read)
	'The %1$s %2$s went back to its state before the run: every part the run wrote was still its own and was put back, and every part reads as the backup after that. Its pair was discarded since the run, so no bases were put back: the object has no pair now. Pair it anew before the next takeover of it (wp_site_pairs action=propose, then confirm).',
	'The %1$s %2$s went back only in part: the object deviated within its step and is left whole, or a part was changed since the run wrote it, was never read back, or needs a check, and is left as it is, or reads other than the backup after the parts went back (see parts; a part left names its value before). Its pair was discarded since the run, so no bases were put back and there is no pair to mark unclear: check the object in wp-admin, then pair it anew (wp_site_pairs action=propose, then confirm).',
	'The parts of the %1$s %2$s were put back as far as they say (see parts), but its pair could not be read, so nothing of the pair was written and this step is not done: the pair keeps the bases the run gave it. List the pairs (wp_site_pairs action=list); once the pair reads again, align it anew (wp_site_pairs action=propose, then confirm) before the next takeover of this object. %3$s',
	// includes/sync/class-sync-code-kind.php (Z8b branch 5: the rights of a step of the code, E10)
	'This site does not let WordPress change its files (DISALLOW_FILE_MODS in wp-config.php, or a filter on file_mod_allowed), so no plugin and no theme is taken over here. Ask the host or the site administrator to lift the setting, or update the plugin or theme by hand over SFTP.',
	'WordPress does not write files directly on this site (its file system method is not direct), and a plugin or theme is taken over by renaming folders, which only the direct method does. Ask the host to let PHP write the folders of plugins and themes as their owner, or update it by hand in wp-admin.',
	'Not taken over: this account may not change the files of the theme %1$s on this site in this way (%2$s; with DISALLOW_FILE_EDIT nobody has edit_themes, which the same version with other files takes).',
	'Not taken over: this account may not change the files of the plugin %1$s on this site in this way (%2$s; with DISALLOW_FILE_EDIT nobody has edit_plugins, which the same version with other files takes).',
	'Abort the run first with its own account and connection (wp_site_push action=abort), then plan a new one (wp_site_push action=plan), without this entry where it stays refused.',
	// includes/sync/class-sync-push.php (Z8b branch 5: a unit of code is no step of the contents, E19)
	'A plugin or theme is taken over by a run of the code of its own, which holds no step of the contents: plan it without the entries of the contents, by its number in select (and in accept where its code runs on this site). all=true leaves it out.',
	// includes/sync/class-sync-code-ops.php (Z8b branch 5: a step of the code in a run, its stage and its check, a journal or a plan that does not read)
	'The plan of this run names no unit of code for step %d in the form a run of the code holds it, so the step does not run and nothing of this site changed. Abort the run (wp_site_push action=abort), make a new report (wp_site_diff) and plan again.',
	'This site already has the %1$s %2$s as the staging site has it (the same files), so nothing is staged and nothing of it is swapped. Make a new report (wp_site_diff): where it still shows the unit as changed, confirm its pair anew (wp_site_pairs).',
	'The stage did not answer in the form a step of the code takes (its group, tree and hash).',
	'The %1$s %2$s of the staging site is staged in the protected store (%3$d files, from %4$s); nothing of this site changed. Its PHP files are checked next: call action=next again.',
	'The stage of the %1$s %2$s is being checked: %3$d of %4$d PHP files so far; nothing of this site changed. Call action=next again.',
	'The %1$s %2$s of the staging site is staged and checked (%3$d PHP files): it is ready for its swap, the next step. Nothing of this site changed.',
	'The %1$s %2$s is not staged (%3$s), so it is not swapped; nothing of this site changed. %4$s',
	'The run goes on with the next step (action=next).',
	'%1$s Step %2$d stays planned, and no unit is swapped without a stage read as ready; nothing of this site changed. Call action=next again; where it keeps failing, abort the run (wp_site_push action=abort).',
	'The journal of step %d does not read as a step of the code wrote it (its unit, its stage, or the answer of its check), so nothing is staged or swapped on it and nothing of this site changed. Abort the run (wp_site_push action=abort), make a new report (wp_site_diff) and plan again.',
	// includes/sync/class-sync-code-plan.php (Z8b branch 5: the plan of a run of the code, its locks and its preview, accept, the binding of its packages)
	'accept names entries, but the selection names no plugin and no theme: accept releases the swap of a unit of code whose code runs on this site, by the number of its entry in select. Leave accept out, or select the unit.',
	'A run of the code holds no step of the contents: code can change what the contents are compared by (the theme, the types a plugin registers). Plan the plugins and themes alone (their numbers in select, without all, choices and as_draft), run that plan to its end, make a new report (wp_site_diff), then plan the contents.',
	'Entry %d is in accept but is no plugin or theme chosen in select: accept releases a unit of code chosen there. Name it in select as well, or leave it out of accept.',
	'The package %s is no package of code taken over here, and a run of the code takes only those (packages may stay empty where every unit comes from wordpress.org). Export the files the preview names on the staging site (wp_site_export with purpose=code and this report_hash), take the package over here (wp_site_import_chunk), then plan again.',
	'Nothing of the selection is taken over: no unit of code chosen is one a run swaps now. %s Use the way each of them names, then plan again (wp_site_push action=plan).',
	'The units of code of this plan do not read in the form a run of the code holds them (the packages of the environment of the report, a name or a hash of a unit), so no run is made. Take the environment of the staging site over anew, make a new report (wp_site_diff) and plan again.',
	'Entry %d of the report does not read in the form a report of this version writes (its subtype, ref or action), so no unit of it is planned and nothing of this site changed. Make a new report (wp_site_diff) and plan again.',
	'The version of this unit is not known on this site, on the staging site or on both (its head names none, or names one that is no version), so whether the staging site has an older version is not known and it is not taken over (code:version_unknown). Give the plugin or theme a Version in its head on both sites, make a new report (wp_site_diff) and plan again; or update it by hand in wp-admin.',
	'The staging site has an older version of this unit (%1$s) than this site (%2$s), and a takeover never goes down a version (code:downgrade). Update it on the staging site, take its environment over anew, make a new report (wp_site_diff) and plan again.',
	'Whether the theme %2$s of entry %1$d runs on this site could not be read (the options stylesheet and template do not read in the form WordPress writes them, or the theme was switched while they were read), so it is not taken over, with accept or without (code:runs_unknown): accept releases code that is read to run, never a state not read. Check the theme of this site in wp-admin (Appearance), then make a new report (wp_site_diff) and plan again.',
	'Whether the plugin %2$s of entry %1$d runs on this site could not be read (the option active_plugins does not read in the form WordPress writes it), so it is not taken over, with accept or without (code:runs_unknown): accept releases code that is read to run, never a state not read. Check the plugins of this site in wp-admin (deactivating and activating one makes WordPress write the option anew), then make a new report (wp_site_diff) and plan again.',
	'not on this site, %s on the staging site',
	'version %1$s here, %2$s on the staging site',
	'Entry %1$d swaps code this site runs: the theme %2$s is the theme that runs or its parent, %3$s. It is taken over only with its number in accept, by which the person releases code of it to run in the swap, its new version too; files come back through the way back, what its routines change in the database does not. Pass accept with this number, or leave the entry out.',
	'Entry %1$d swaps code this site runs: the plugin %2$s is active, %3$s. It is taken over only with its number in accept, by which the person releases code of it to run in the swap, its new version too; files come back through the way back, what its routines change in the database does not. Pass accept with this number, or leave the entry out.',
	'This site already has the unit as the staging site has it (the same files), so nothing of it is taken over. Make a new report (wp_site_diff): where it still shows the unit as changed, confirm its pair anew (wp_site_pairs).',
	'The report does not hold every path of this unit that lies on this site and is not in the version of the staging site (its list only_live and the entries more_paths after it do not read whole), and the preview names each of them before a swap, so it is not taken over (code:paths_unknown). Make a new report (wp_site_diff) and plan again.',
	'Files come back through the way back; what the routines of the new version change in the database does not.',
	'Every path of this unit on this site is in the new version as well.',
	'These paths lie on this site and are not in the new version: after the swap each of them lies in the backup, back through the way back.',
	'No package of code was passed: the unit comes from wordpress.org in the exact version of the staging site, taken only where it is the unit the report compared. Where it is not from wordpress.org, export these paths on the staging site (wp_site_export with purpose=code, this unit and its paths; without paths every file), take the package over here and pass it in packages.',
	'The unit is built from the packages of code passed and from the files this site has already; the stage needs these paths from a package.',
	'The package %s of this plan is no longer in the protected store, so the run of the code cannot keep it until its swaps. Take the environment (and the packages of code) of the staging site over anew, make a new report (wp_site_diff) and plan again.',
	// includes/sync/class-sync-push.php (Z8b branch 5: accept, a run of the code closed at once, the description of the run)
	'accept is a list of entry numbers of the report: the plugins and themes chosen in select whose code runs on this site and whose swap the person releases.',
	'%1$s Run %2$d was made for this plan and closed again as aborted at once: nothing was staged or written. Call wp_site_push action=plan again once the packages are there.',
	'Makes a run of the code: each plugin or theme named is staged in the protected store first (nothing of this site changes), then swapped in one call under the lock of AlphaBridge, with a probe of the site before and the old version kept whole in the backup. A plugin or theme new on this site is refused at its swap in this version (code:create_not_built). The run holds no step of the contents: make a new report (wp_site_diff) after it. Nothing is written by this call; the confirmed call makes the run.',
	// includes/sync/class-sync-code-plan.php, includes/sync/class-sync-engine.php (Z8b branch 5, 1a-3: a pair not named in its form, a plan of a run that does not read back in its check)
	'Entry %d of the report names no pair in the form a report of this version writes it (a whole number of 1 or more), so its unit is not taken over and nothing of this site changed. Make a new report (wp_site_diff) and plan again.',
	'The plan of this run does not read back, so step %d is judged neither as a step of the code nor as an object, and nothing of it counts as taken over. Check the site as it is in wp-admin; where the run is still open, abort it (wp_site_push action=abort).',
	// includes/sync/class-sync-code-ops.php, includes/sync/class-sync-code-plan.php (Z8b branch 5, K1a: a ready stage not bound to its step (A2), a group of the packages not of its form)
	'The stage the journal of this step names is not bound to this run, this unit and the version of the staging site the plan names, so this step is not done on it. Abort the run (wp_site_push action=abort), make a new report (wp_site_diff) and plan again.',
	// includes/sync/class-sync-code-plan.php (Z8b branch 5, K1b: the paths that go into the backup read now (A1): not read whole, not those of the report).
	'The files of this unit on this site could not be read whole now, and the preview names each path of it that is not in the version of the staging site before a swap, so it is not taken over (code:paths_unread). Where the time of this call did not suffice, plan again (wp_site_push action=plan). Where the lock stays, a file or folder of the plugin or theme here cannot be read: make it readable, then plan again; where the unit is no longer on this site, make a new report (wp_site_diff).',
	'The paths of this unit on this site that are not in the version of the staging site are not those of the report any more (a file was added here or removed since the report was made), and the preview names each of them before a swap, so it is not taken over (code:paths_changed). Make a new report (wp_site_diff), then plan again.',
	// includes/sync/class-sync-code-stage.php (Z8b branch 5, K2: the binding of a stage held by the stage (A2, option A): a binding not of its form, an entry of its group not of its form).
	// includes/class-protected-store.php (Z8b branch 5, K2: the entry of a group read by its id, AB_MCP_Protected_Store::entry()).
	'The entry of the group could not be read whole in the protected store (its sidecar cannot be read, is not there, or is not of its form), so what the group is bound to is not known. Try again; if it keeps failing, ask the host to check the rights of the folder.',
	// includes/class-protected-store.php (Z8b branch 5, K4d: a group that group() does not give, gone or there and not read, one text for both, AB_MCP_Protected_Store::no_group(); it replaces the text of K4. K4e: without the sentence on what the call changed. K4f: without the periods groups are kept).
	'The group could not be read in the protected store, and the store does not tell which of these is why. It is not there: it was never opened here (a group belongs to the area it was opened in), or it was removed. Or it is still there, but its entry (its sidecar) is missing, is no plain file, cannot be read, is not of its form or names another group, or its folder is missing or cannot be reached. Where it is gone, open a new one with open(). Where it should still be there, try again; if it keeps failing, ask the host to check the folder of the protected store and the rights on it.',
	// includes/class-protected-store.php (Z8b branch 5, K4f and K4g: a file not found or not inspected in its group, AB_MCP_Protected_Store::get(); one text for every area, with no cause claimed as the only one and the way of each case; it replaces the text of K4f).
	'The file was not found in its group of the protected store, or it could not be inspected there; the store does not tell which. Where it belongs to a package or a report whose source is still there, make that anew. A backup of what a run already replaced cannot be made anew: check the object in wp-admin, or ask the host whether a backup of the site holds it. Where the file should still be there, ask the host to check the folder of the protected store and the rights on it.',
	// includes/sync/class-sync-code-ops.php (Z8b branch 5, part 2a)
	'Whether code of the %1$s %2$s runs on this site could not be read now (the options active_plugins, stylesheet and template do not read in the form WordPress writes them, or the theme was switched while they were read), so it is not swapped. Check the plugins and the theme of this site in wp-admin (deactivating and activating a plugin makes WordPress write the option anew), then call action=next again; or abort the run (wp_site_push action=abort).',
	'Code of the %1$s %2$s runs on this site now, and the plan of this run does not release it (its number was not in accept), so it is not swapped. Deactivate it in wp-admin (or switch to another theme) and call action=next again; or abort the run (wp_site_push action=abort), make a new report (wp_site_diff) and plan again with its number in accept.',
	// includes/sync/class-sync-code-swap.php (Z8b branch 5, part 2a)
	'OPcache runs on this site, and this request may not take a PHP file out of it (opcache.restrict_api, or the filter wp_opcache_invalidate_file), so running code is not swapped: the site could go on running the old code. Ask the host to let WordPress clear OPcache (opcache.restrict_api), or update the unit by hand in wp-admin.',
	'Whether this request can take a PHP file out of OPcache could not be read (its answer is none of invalidated, not_active and not_possible), so running code is not swapped. Call action=next again; where it keeps failing, update the unit by hand in wp-admin.',
	'The lock for changes of the code is not read as held by this request (its answer, or its row in the database, is not of its form), so nothing is swapped. Call action=next again; where it keeps failing, check that the database of this site accepts writes.',
	'The swap was asked with values not of its form (the run, the unit of its step, the packages of the environment, the stage and the time of the call), so nothing is taken and nothing is swapped. Abort the run (wp_site_push action=abort), make a new report (wp_site_diff) and plan again.',
	'This site has no folder for plugins or themes WordPress names, so nothing is swapped. Check the constants WP_PLUGIN_DIR and the theme folder in wp-config.php.',
