	'The test requests of AlphaBridge are switched off on this site (the filter ab_mcp_php_probe_enabled), or not read as switched on, so the %1$s %2$s is not swapped: nothing would show that the site works before the swap. Switch the test requests on again, or update the unit by hand in wp-admin.',
	'Whether the place of the %1$s %2$s on this site, which the plan makes new here, is empty could not be read now (its folder was not listed, or the place not read), so it is not swapped. Call action=next again; where it keeps failing, ask the host why the folder of the plugins or themes cannot be read.',
	'AlphaBridge\'s lock for changes of the code, which this call took, could not be given back, so it stays: other changes through AlphaBridge can be refused until it is %d minutes old; from then on the next one takes it over.',
	// includes/lifecycle/class-change-lock.php (Z8b branch 5, part 2a, the lead after the Codex round on the order of the Behebung: the lock for changes held, its holders as examples, no change and nothing running claimed; it replaces the text with the swap among the changes).
	'Not started: AlphaBridge\'s lock for changes of the code this site runs is held, and who holds it cannot be told here. Every change through AlphaBridge that takes this lock waits for it, so that the way back of one cannot undo the other. It is taken, for example, by an activation, an update, a deploy, a swap of a plugin or theme from the staging site, a PHP file or snippet written or undone, a call of wp_site_push on its run (a step, an abort, a reading of its state) and the closing of a journal of the site address; a request that ended early can have left it behind. Nothing was changed; call again in a few minutes. Once its time is %d minutes old, the next call takes it over.',
	'Its time was written at %s UTC.',
	// includes/sync/class-sync-deadline.php (Z8b branch 5, R12 part 1: the deadline of the readings of a swap; its end, its clock unknown, a deadline that is none).
